On this mine site, we have 1,700 acres

472
00:32:40,161 --> 00:32:42,540
and approximately 6 million ton of coal.

473
00:32:42,541 --> 00:32:46,800
We're figuring on being here a little over six years.

474
00:32:46,801 --> 00:32:48,260
During those six years, the loader

475
00:32:48,261 --> 00:32:51,500
will be in operation for roughly 22 hours a day,

476
00:32:51,501 --> 00:32:52,860
at least five days a week.

477
00:32:55,580 --> 00:33:00,820
The goal, to strip at least 1,300 tons of coal each day.

478
00:33:00,821 --> 00:33:05,500
That means moving 26,000 tons of material every day.

479
00:33:05,501 --> 00:33:07,080
My name's Zavrit.

480
00:33:07,081 --> 00:33:09,500
They call me Hop Singh.

481
00:33:09,501 --> 00:33:12,340
That's my CB handle.

482
00:33:12,341 --> 00:33:14,860
I've been doing about 30 years.

483
00:33:14,861 --> 00:33:16,500
Been with this place about six.

484
00:33:18,260 --> 00:33:21,340
He has got a truck to him at all times,

485
00:33:21,900 --> 00:33:27,580
and he just goes in, makes a short pass, and loads the truck.

486
00:33:27,700 --> 00:33:30,140
He's running about a 30-second cycle time,

487
00:33:30,500 --> 00:33:33,980
and he's putting anywhere from four to five buckets per truck.

488
00:33:35,580 --> 00:33:38,540
When I go in to dig, I've got to keep hoist up,

489
00:33:39,200 --> 00:33:41,440
keep pressure on the wheels so it won't spin.

490
00:33:42,760 --> 00:33:45,240
Of course, the bucket is the business end of the beast.

491
00:33:45,241 --> 00:33:56,320
The 994 bucket is 19 feet wide, 10 foot tall, holds 27 yards of dirt, which is approximately

492
00:33:56,321 --> 00:33:57,320
40 ton.

493
00:33:57,321 --> 00:34:02,120
It would take 10 wheelbarrows to make a yard of dirt.

494
00:34:02,121 --> 00:34:08,340
So you're looking at 270 to 300 wheelbarrows to fill this bucket.

495
00:34:08,341 --> 00:34:12,320
This machine burns approximately 45 gallon of fuel per hour.

496
00:34:12,321 --> 00:34:15,720
It has a 1,000-gallon tank on it, so we fuel it every day.

497
00:34:17,080 --> 00:34:20,560
Operating this big caterpillar requires 1,500 horsepower

498
00:34:20,561 --> 00:34:23,080
to drive its hydraulics and transmission.

499
00:34:24,440 --> 00:34:28,380
Your everyday automobile has approximately 200 horsepower.

500
00:34:29,120 --> 00:34:32,080
You can't just drive a behemoth like this to the work site.

501
00:34:33,360 --> 00:34:37,320
The machine is manufactured in Aurora, Illinois,

502
00:34:37,321 --> 00:34:47,320
and load it on a number of rail cars or 11 or 12 semi trucks for transportation to a site like here in Cadiz.

503
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:54,660
Once it arrives at its destination, assembly requires several trains and over 400 man hours.

504
00:34:55,260 --> 00:35:01,060
I have the privilege of working with and seeing loaders that are tiny and others that are huge.

505
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:02,420
This loader's massive.

506
00:35:02,421 --> 00:35:08,020
Not so massive is Compact Power's Boxer Mini Skid Loader.

507
00:35:12,520 --> 00:35:18,100
The small size allows do-it-yourselfers and contractors to work in smaller, more sensitive areas.

508
00:35:21,920 --> 00:35:30,780
The mini skid weighs 240 times less than the Cat 994F, and more than 30 of them could easily be scooped into the big guy's bucket.

509
00:35:32,420 --> 00:35:38,800
I'm standing on the Boxer Mini Skid, which weighs about 2,000 pounds, which is a third

510
00:35:38,801 --> 00:35:44,220
of the average skid steer loader, and has a very light footprint because of the rubber

511
00:35:44,221 --> 00:35:46,260
track system underneath the unit.

512
00:35:46,261 --> 00:35:51,320
So you can take it almost anywhere with minimal damage to the terrain.

513
00:35:51,321 --> 00:35:57,980
The Boxer has a unique feature which allows you to widen your tracks out to about 42 inches

514
00:35:57,981 --> 00:36:04,980
to provide stability on slopes, but it also allows you to narrow the tracks underneath

515
00:36:04,981 --> 00:36:08,980
three feet wide to go through a narrow gate.

516
00:36:08,981 --> 00:36:14,220
Don't let this little loader deceive you.

517
00:36:14,221 --> 00:36:21,740
Its 32 horsepower engine provides it with enough hydraulic power to lift its own weight.

518
00:36:21,741 --> 00:36:25,040
Being small has another advantage.

519
00:36:25,041 --> 00:36:27,340
can run nearly 100 different attachments

520
00:36:27,341 --> 00:36:29,780
that are fairly easy to switch out.

521
00:36:29,781 --> 00:36:32,480
It's almost like an extension of your own body,

522
00:36:32,481 --> 00:36:35,420
that you can do things with this machine

523
00:36:35,421 --> 00:36:38,880
that you can never imagine trying to do with your own power.

524
00:36:38,881 --> 00:36:41,820
I like to think about the Boxer as my own little muscle man

525
00:36:41,821 --> 00:36:45,800
that follows me around to do all my hard work for me.

526
00:36:45,801 --> 00:36:49,660
This little muscle man may get your job done,

527
00:36:49,661 --> 00:36:54,040
but its 32 horsepower won't propel this container ship.

528
00:36:54,041 --> 00:36:57,080
You'll need one of the biggest diesel engines in the world for that.

529
00:37:01,180 --> 00:37:03,920
Diesel engines vary enormously in size.

530
00:37:06,860 --> 00:37:10,620
Take, for example, the one that powers the behemoth Chicago Bridge.

531
00:37:11,420 --> 00:37:13,940
It's among the largest container ships in the world.

532
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:20,040
Without a super-sized diesel engine to match, this mammoth ship is dead in the water.

533
00:37:20,041 --> 00:37:28,100
This ship is quite a big ship, and it's about 50,000 tons of cargo you're carrying.

534
00:37:28,240 --> 00:37:30,120
So for that, you require a huge engine.

535
00:37:31,080 --> 00:37:36,600
Within the hull of the ship is just that, the 10K98MC.

536
00:37:40,840 --> 00:37:45,820
This three-story tall, 1,850-ton, 10-cylinder powerhouse

537
00:37:45,821 --> 00:37:49,700
was developed by the biggest supplier of large diesels in the world.

538
00:37:50,040 --> 00:37:51,160
manned diesel.

539
00:37:52,680 --> 00:37:56,280
The engine is developing approximately 78,000 horsepower,

540
00:37:56,720 --> 00:38:02,080
which is equivalent to the horsepower in approximately 170 semi-trucks.

541
00:38:02,500 --> 00:38:10,200
The size of the engine is approximately 25 feet wide, 66 feet long, 44 feet tall.

542
00:38:10,900 --> 00:38:12,680
It's a very, very big engine.

543
00:38:13,960 --> 00:38:17,880
Buried within this 10-cylinder beast are 10 enormous pistons.

544
00:38:17,881 --> 00:38:23,080
The weight of the piston is approximately 5.5 tons.

545
00:38:23,800 --> 00:38:27,380
This little baby is approximately 20 feet tall.

546
00:38:28,580 --> 00:38:37,580
Unlike internal combustion engines, all diesel engines rely on the piston to compress the air inside the cylinder until it becomes extremely hot.

547
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:46,460
So when fuel is injected, it quickly ignites, and the explosion forces the piston back down again.

548
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:54,020
That piston is connected to the crankshaft which rotates and rotates the propeller shaft

549
00:38:54,021 --> 00:38:55,620
and brings the ship through the water.

550
00:38:57,900 --> 00:39:03,820
When shut off, engineers can step into the middle area of the engine, called the scavenger space.

551
00:39:05,480 --> 00:39:08,120
Here they can inspect the piston rings and rods.

552
00:39:09,240 --> 00:39:13,180
But to see how the engine really works involves going to the bottom.

553
00:39:14,020 --> 00:39:17,300
Right now the engine is turned by a device called the turning gear.

554
00:39:17,301 --> 00:39:21,960
It's rotating the crankshaft, moving the pistons up and down.

555
00:39:22,700 --> 00:39:24,340
But this is very slow, of course.

556
00:39:24,900 --> 00:39:29,740
But when the engine is running, it's moving up and down 94 times a minute.

557
00:39:30,340 --> 00:39:33,620
When the engine is running, there's a lot of oil splashing around in here.

558
00:39:33,900 --> 00:39:39,440
Thousands of gallons of oil is run through the engine every hour for lubrication and cooling down.

559
00:39:40,220 --> 00:39:44,300
To keep this mighty marvel running requires 200 tons of fuel a day.

560
00:39:45,260 --> 00:39:47,440
That's 43,000 gallons.

561
00:39:48,520 --> 00:39:51,320
This ship can load over 5,000 containers,

562
00:39:51,760 --> 00:39:54,420
so it's carrying that kind of load with 25 knots

563
00:39:54,421 --> 00:39:56,520
and using only 200 tons a day.

564
00:39:56,660 --> 00:39:57,680
That's not so bad.

565
00:39:58,280 --> 00:40:00,960
While there are a handful of diesels bigger than this,

566
00:40:01,620 --> 00:40:03,960
most diesel engines would be dwarfed in its presence.

567
00:40:05,140 --> 00:40:08,540
One of them is on your television screen right now.

568
00:40:09,100 --> 00:40:09,800
Can you see it?

569
00:40:10,160 --> 00:40:10,860
Look closely.

570
00:40:10,861 --> 00:40:15,740
this tiny model airplane engine is no bigger than one of this big boy's bolts.

571
00:40:18,280 --> 00:40:21,160
While it only produces about one-third of a horsepower,

572
00:40:21,720 --> 00:40:24,160
that's plenty to run a small model airplane.

573
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:32,480
Few people know model engines like Randy Lincolato.

574
00:40:33,600 --> 00:40:38,320
His company, KMB Manufacturing, is the largest American model engine builder.

575
00:40:39,240 --> 00:40:42,200
They make engines for both model boats and airplanes.

576
00:40:43,240 --> 00:40:45,620
I started doing this 30 years ago.

577
00:40:46,120 --> 00:40:48,440
I got into the business because I really loved engines.

578
00:40:48,980 --> 00:40:51,680
I thought that was the greatest thing to try to make engines.

579
00:40:52,740 --> 00:40:57,540
A model diesel engine works almost like its gargantuan cousin, with one big exception.

580
00:40:58,460 --> 00:41:07,860
The difference between the regular diesel and a model diesel is the model diesel uses a carburetor to have a fuel-air mixture go into the engine.

581
00:41:08,320 --> 00:41:11,100
where an actual diesel engine uses a fuel injector.

582
00:41:12,540 --> 00:41:15,020
But its basic operation looks pretty familiar.

583
00:41:16,280 --> 00:41:19,640
Once the combustion occurs, it forces the piston downward,

584
00:41:19,900 --> 00:41:22,840
which moves the crankshaft and in turn turns the propeller

585
00:41:22,841 --> 00:41:25,440
and moves the plane through the air.

586
00:41:26,480 --> 00:41:30,460
Like bigger diesels, model diesel engines also come in various sizes.

587
00:41:31,800 --> 00:41:34,360
Even in the world of model engines, there's big and small.

588
00:41:34,860 --> 00:41:37,300
This is a cylinder and piston out of our biggest engine,

589
00:41:37,301 --> 00:41:39,220
which is about one cubic inch.

590
00:41:41,100 --> 00:41:43,760
And this is a piston cylinder of our smallest engine.

591
00:41:45,380 --> 00:41:49,980
K&B manufactures almost all the small engine parts here on Precision Equipment.

592
00:41:50,860 --> 00:41:53,580
The smaller the engine, the more precise it has to be.

593
00:41:54,080 --> 00:41:56,160
They carefully hand-assemble each engine.

594
00:41:56,840 --> 00:41:59,500
We work with real small tools, real small parts.

595
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:04,540
It's basically just like a car engine except there's just one cylinder and it's small.

596
00:42:04,541 --> 00:42:07,380
You can't make any mistakes. Everything's got to be perfect.

597
00:42:07,580 --> 00:42:11,840
Now, you've got one part that's 1,000th off, and you have to start all over again.

598
00:42:12,640 --> 00:42:15,660
I make about maybe between 100 to 50, 200 a day.

599
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:18,260
On a good day, I can do about 225.

600
00:42:19,320 --> 00:42:23,520
Unlike regular diesel engines, the model engines run on a special fuel blend.

601
00:42:24,620 --> 00:42:28,180
We're going to run this on a mixture of ether, kerosene, and oil, equal parts.

602
00:42:28,900 --> 00:42:31,240
Now that it's all fueled up, it's ready to go.

603
00:42:31,241 --> 00:42:35,620
Normally you wouldn't use your fingers to start an engine, but I've been doing this

604
00:42:35,621 --> 00:42:37,200
for so many years.

605
00:42:37,201 --> 00:42:42,840
I'm old school, what can I say?

606
00:42:42,841 --> 00:42:55,300
But the fun starts when the engine meets the plane.

607
00:42:55,301 --> 00:43:00,300
For Andy, there's nothing like the distinctive hum of a model airplane.

608
00:43:00,301 --> 00:43:05,300
The sound of these small precision engines is music to my ears.

609
00:43:05,301 --> 00:43:15,300
It may not be an Airbus A380, but in the world of the big and small, there's plenty of room to accommodate both.

